A||||5||GREENDANO||Engine compartment color?
Z||000000||GREENDANO||04-01-99||07:02 PM||||I'm adding a PISA fastback as well as changing the color of my GT.  Question....What color is everyones' engine compartment and underhood color.  Can I assume it's the same as body color?  I wanted to check to sort-of be factory correct, even though it's a custom fastback.<br>  Also, You guys with the Yellow 88's, what color is all your ground effects?  Also would like personal opinions on choice of body color or silver for ground effects<br>  Dan-O
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||04-02-99||12:27 AM||||The engine compartment and underhood color is always black, at least as far as I know.
Z||000002||Motorhead||04-02-99||03:58 AM||||Back in 1984, my factory fresh engine compartment was BLACK.
Z||000003||theogre||04-02-99||09:57 AM||||In every Fiero i've seen, of every year...... they are all black. They were painted before the panels go on. GM is cheap. It's all black, except for body pannels, and interior.  The back side if most pannels are either unfinished, or black, on most of the cars I've seen.<p>Most of the exterior trim I've seen, except the side moldings, matches the body.
Z||000004||GREENDANO||04-02-99||07:45 PM||||The reason I was asking about ground effects color is because my 85 GT has silver ground effects and I was looking for suggestions and/or pictures on which color to make them<br>   Dan-O
Z||000005||theogre||04-03-99||10:38 PM||||well...... that probably varied by year. The GT I was looking at just the other day has everything pretty much the same goldish/tannish color. I think it was an 86, I didn't have time to collect the vin.
